module gunbc.guarantee_stall.roster_re_enumerates_its_own_rows_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { OutsideTheLadder, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, ClimbableButUnbuilt, UncountedNotEnumerable }

// WHY THE BLOCKER IS `ClimbableButUnbuilt` WHEN THE CEILING AWAITS A GROUNDING, which is the one
// thing a reader of this row is likeliest to read as a contradiction. DESIGN section 4b(2) obliges
// a stall to separate "cannot climb further" from "can climb after one grounding" from "can climb
// NOW but unbuilt", and that classification is about THIS ROW'S STANDING STATE -- whether it can
// move off the rung it sits on -- not about the last step to its ceiling. This class sits OUTSIDE
// THE LADDER and the climb off it needs no capability that does not exist today, so it is
// climbable and unbuilt. Calling it `AwaitsOneGrounding` because the CEILING needs one would put an
// affordable climb behind a capability nobody is building, and would assert the third case is the
// second -- the misclassification this paragraph exists to prevent, caught in review of the first
// version of this row (gunbc#10366, review 59852) where the blocker contradicted the evidence six
// lines above it.
//
// THE CEILING'S GROUNDING THEREFORE LIVES IN THIS ANNOTATION AND NOT IN A FIELD, recorded as a
// limit of the carrier rather than left for a reader to notice as an omission. `GuaranteeStall`
// carries ONE `blocker`, which answers for the immediate climb, and `ceiling` is a bare
// `GuaranteeRung` with nothing attached; there is no field in which "what the LAST step needs" can
// be written, so it is written here. It is: declaration introspection sufficient to BIND a
// discovered data declaration as a typed value of its declared type -- not merely to report that it
// exists, its name, or its declared type as strings -- such that a roster is folded over the
// declared population with no authored name per row, at which point an unrostered row has no
// constructor because there is no list to omit it from. Stated as BINDING and not as introspection
// deliberately: a trigger naming discovery would be satisfied by `data_decl_type_facts`, which
// already exists, while the capability it is meant to restore stayed dead -- the DESIGN section
// 4b(3) failure of a trigger naming less than it restores. This paragraph is not evidence that
// anything holds; no Accepted program reads it (section 4c). It is the honest home for a fact the
// type cannot carry, and if a later lane gives the ceiling its own grounding field, this is the row
// whose prose moves into it.
//
// THE TWO CAPABILITIES ARE SEPARABLE AND ONLY ONE IS MISSING, measured rather than assumed.
// MEMBERSHIP discovery EXISTS: `v2.std.decl_index` `data_decl_type_facts` returns module path,
// declaration name and declared type per top-level `data` declaration, so the declared population of
// a rostered row type is derivable today and a declared-versus-rostered identity join is affordable
// without any new capability. VALUE BINDING DOES NOT EXIST, and it is what a DERIVED roster needs:
// `decl_facts` yields `node: Node`, the initializer projection -- a syntax tree, which that module's
// own annotation records as dropping the declared type -- and there is no glob or derived import, so
// a value is bound only by an authored name. Decoding a typed value out of a data initializer is
// already declared blocked in a second carrier: `test.fixture.scaffold_disposition_census.pool_notes`
// records the same constructor/variant-value identity prerequisite as the reason nothing there
// decodes a `Disposition`. This separability is what the paragraph above rests on: it is why the
// blocker can be `ClimbableButUnbuilt` while the ceiling still awaits a grounding.
//
// THE DEMAND PREDATES THIS ROW, which is what keeps it from being self-serving. `std.primitives`
// `primitive_contract_roster_note` independently names this class and this dissolution for its own
// contract roster -- "derive the roster by enumerating *_contract declarations once declaration
// introspection lands, so contract surfaces read the module rather than a second list" -- and
// `gunbc.ci.ci_spec` names the same capability again, as does `std.primitive_identity`. None was
// authored for this lane.
//
// THIS ROW DEMONSTRATES ITS OWN SUBJECT ON THE WAY IN, recorded because it is evidence and not an
// embarrassment: filing it appends one import and one entry to `gunbc.guarantee_stall.roster`, which
// is one of the carriers the subject is about. The population is not theoretical.
//
// HOW THE POPULATION WAS SEARCHED, stated because a bounded population whose discovery method is
// unstated cannot be told from the carriers someone happened to grep. The executed rule over every
// non-test `.dag` in `dag/` and `src/`: a module that imports at least five declarations by name AND
// enumerates at least five of those same names again as bare entries of a list literal. It returned
// thirteen carriers, headed by this carrier's own roster and by
// `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster`. TWO BLIND SPOTS ARE KNOWN AND NAMED. It UNDER-reports: the
// `std.primitives` contract roster is intra-module, so its second enumeration imports nothing and
// the rule cannot see it, and the same holds for every future roster of same-module rows. It
// OVER-reports: a list literal of imported names is not necessarily a second enumeration of a
// rostered population. So the count is a proxy over a class that gains a member whenever a carrier
// splits into per-row files, which is why the population is UNCOUNTED rather than a list of
// thirteen: rendering that list would read as "these are affected", the selection-view-read-as-
// population narrow, when the real exposure is every per-row carrier that exists or will.
data roster_re_enumerates_its_own_rows_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "a roster of per-module rows enumerates by hand the declarations it rosters, so a declared row absent from the list is silently absent from every projection derived from it",
  current: OutsideTheLadder,
  ceiling: StructurallyImpossible,
  blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
  population: UncountedNotEnumerable { reason: "every carrier whose rows live one per module and are re-enumerated in a roster, a class that gains a member whenever a carrier splits into per-row files; an executed proxy over non-test dag/ and src/ modules importing at least five names and re-listing at least five of them returned thirteen carriers on the derivation base named in the PR body, which under-reports intra-module rosters such as the std.primitives contract roster and over-reports any list literal of imported names, so it bounds nothing" },
  next_rung_trigger: "a declared-versus-rostered identity join executing as a merge-blocking check on every rostered row type -- the declared population read through v2.std.decl_index data_decl_type_facts, joined at declaration identity rather than at count, refusing with the located identity of each declared row the roster omits -- which needs no capability that does not exist today and leaves the invalid state writable, hence mechanically preventable and not the ceiling"
}
